/-!
# Theorem 2.2, existence: strong solutions give an evolution (Yamada–Watanabe)

Packet PROVE-SEC2-PATCH2. For a separated force word (`∀ i j, xL i < xR j`), if Wiener-almost
every continuous path drives a solution of Definition 2.1 (with maximal lifetime), then an
integrated `SLE_a(ρ)` evolution exists (`exists_isIntegratedSLEEvolution_of_ae_mem`): the frozen
conclusion of `exists_isIntegratedSLEEvolution` for this word.

Construction (added here; it is the Yamada–Watanabe principle "pathwise uniqueness + solutions
for almost every path ⇒ strong solution", with the filtration generated by the solution):

* the probability space is `CPath` with the Wiener measure, `B` the coordinate process;
* the solution of the path `f` is `solCode (encC f)`: by pathwise uniqueness
  (`injOn_fst_cRel`) and Lusin–Souslin the driving-code projection of the canonical solution codes
  is a measurable embedding, and `solCode` is its measurable inverse;
* the filtration `solFiltration` is generated by `B` and the killed state;
* `B` is a Brownian motion in it: every event of `solFiltration s` is saturated at `s` on the set of
  paths with a solution (two solutions driven by paths that agree on `[0, s]` have the same killed
  state up to `s`, `IsIntegratedSLEPath.killed_agree_of_eqOn`), so it is independent of the later
  increments (`indep_increment_of_le_satSpace`).
-/

set_option autoImplicit false

noncomputable section

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory Set Filter Topology
open scoped NNReal ENNReal

